a("- D1 (entry timing, T04). Filling at the signal close, the next open or one bar later moves the mean by under 0.001 percentage point (-0.0090, -0.0089, -0.0083, se 0.0037). For this rule the delay does not matter, so this cell is CLEARED for a 30-bar hold. It is not cleared for the 27 testnet layers, because execution/ records no decision price (brief 1c).")
a("- D2 (intrabar order, C05). At the stop sizes the traders state (0.044%/0.088%), 3.27% of all 1m bars could hit both stop and target, and 30.6% reach the stop inside the entry bar. At 0.10/0.20 it is 0.37% and 10.5%. Any 1m simulator with tight stops must pick an order inside a bar; T03 tested the engine convention but no study reports its sensitivity to it.")
a("- D3 (multiple arms, S01). With a placebo null, the share of runs where at least one arm passes `gross mean >= 0.14% and t_gross >= 2` is 1.4% for 1 arm, 7.8% for 4, 23.8% for 12, 60.5% for 40. The full net bar (`t_net >= 2`) keeps the rate at 0.00%, 0.10%, 0.10%, 1.00%: the cost is a strong guard. The risk is in the gross stage and in the INCONCLUSIVE and exploratory reads, which have no correction (brief L7).")
a("- D4 (regime drift, R01). Mean 390-bar long-only return by year: 2022 -0.0626%, 2023 +0.0768%, 2024H1 +0.0665%; whole DEV +0.0189%. A 70/30 long/short arm carries 0.4 times that drift (+0.0076% on all DEV, up to +0.031% in 2023). Small against the 0.14% bar but of the size of the DIFF bar (+0.05%) in a good year.")
a("- D5 (volatility-scaled cost, C01). Median 1m range is 5.8 bp, but the bar after a breakout signal has median 8.4 bp, mean 12.5 bp, and 27.7% of entries sit in a bar whose range exceeds the whole 14 bp round-trip cost (15.0% of all bars). With slippage = 10% of the bar range the mean slip is 1.25 bp per fill, below the flat 2 bp, so the flat cost is conservative on average and CLEARED in the mean; the tail (27.7% of entries in fast bars) is not measured.")
